{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Final report — CLI `--output json` js-safe timestamps (RESOLVED)\n\n**Ticket:** e127-a3ad-895a-4a2f (`unhelping-creviced-rhino`, P3) — closed `--class=preexisting` (contract evolution / pre-existing wire-shape gap; no `--caused-by`, no `--force`).\n\n### Outcome\nDefect fully remediated across three merged Gerrit changes:\n- **2347** (`1504d096ceca`) — core `js_safe_dumps` choke point + subset of emitters + `test_cli_js_safe_integers.py` + docs (BREAKING recorded in release-notes/CHANGELOG). Landed in parallel for the same ticket.\n- **2358** (`3642db3b9b21`) — operator-mandated AST guard `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py` (wired into `make lint`) + wiring + sweep of the 49 remaining `--output json` emitter sites through the single converter + guard self-tests.\n- **2364** (`ba7a6bd3d8b0`) — guard hardening: fail-CLOSED on ambiguous `file=`, docstring accuracy, negative-scope / exit-code / ambiguous-file tests.\n\nAll three carry the `rebar-ticket: e127-a3ad-895a-4a2f` trailer + DCO sign-off; each landed with **LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1**.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n1. **Single choke point + guard** — MET. All CLI `--output json` store-data serialization routes through `js_safe_dumps` (applies `js_safe_result` before `json.dumps`). The AST guard fails CI if store data reaches a raw stdout `json.dumps` without the js-safe conversion, mirroring `scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py`. 49 previously-scattered sites converted.\n2. **Declared-int caveat** — VERIFIED. created_at/updated_at/signed_at are emitted from the plain dict path (extra=\"allow\" / post-`model_dump`); the decimal-string wire value does not revert to a bare number via `model_validate`.\n3. **RED-first regression** — MET. `test_cli_js_safe_integers.py` asserts BOTH (a) `int(wire_value) == stored_value` (lossless, no −42ns drift) AND (b) the wire value is a JSON **string**, not a bare number — the direct guard against the `TypeError: Do not know how to serialize a BigInt` failure mode.\n\n### Gates\n- `make lint` (ruff + guard + complexity ratchet new=0), typecheck (685 files), module-size (all <800) — green.\n- The 8 `tests/interfaces` failures observed are PRE-EXISTING on clean origin/main (macOS git-subprocess env issues), NOT regressions — confirmed in a throwaway clean-main worktree.\n\n### Cross-ticket note (REPORT, not acting)\nThe merged guard `scripts/check_cli_json_js_safe.py` substantively satisfies the acceptance criteria of **`spherelike-oily-honeyeater`** (`83eb-c3e1-3dfd-472f`, \"CLI surface cannot drift silently\"), to which the guard was separately delegated. **Recommend 83eb be closed as satisfied by this work** — not closing it here (out of requested scope, not claimed). `guilty-pusslike-wyvern` (`a8db-dc3c-983a-40b0`, export NDJSON boundary, linked `discovered_from`) left unchanged."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787974628902001001,"uuid":"e887d94b-0f4e-44fa-b734-d673845828fd"}